  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message and visual scene implying personal responsibility or shared experience with the stereotype",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you' in the text. However, the meme's structure and overall intent create an implicit projection where the viewer is positioned as someone who understands or accepts the stereotype being presented. The user is projected onto the textual material ('latinos will do anything to get into trump's america') and the visual scene ('border_crossing_scene'), which together form a narrative that the user is expected to interpret as a universal truth or a shared social commentary. This projection is not direct (e.g., 'you are the one climbing') but rather indirect, through the framing of the meme as a statement about a group's supposed behavior, which the user is invited to internalize or react to as part of their worldview.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
